WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.049
If you want to know how Jaws almost killed
the entire town of Amity, including the deaths

00:00:04.049 --> 00:00:07.902
that were taken out of the movie, then stick around
until the end of this video.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.090
Jaws is the beast from the sea that rarely
surfaced in his own movie and but came out

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:20.480
slightly more in the novel, oftentimes leaving
a trail of blood and flesh in his wake.

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:24.580
He was the nightmare laying siege, physically
and mentally, to the small-town of Amity and

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:25.820
their year-round residents.

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:29.880
Jaws author Peter Benchley stated that he
“could never write Jaws today” or “demonize

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:33.070
an animal” Since Jaws is a shark, we’re
going to look at what makes him the demon

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:34.700
that Benchley originally intended.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:38.460
So, in today’s episode, we’ll attempt
to analyze the shark’s impact on Amity through

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:39.960
a psychological lens.

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:44.059
To understand the full threat of the shark’s
occupation, we've gotta start by understanding

00:00:44.059 --> 00:00:45.450
the town.

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:52.930
Amity is one of the summer communities on
Long Island’s southern shore.

00:00:52.930 --> 00:00:57.180
The population of its year-round residents
is about 1,000, boosting to 10,000 in the

00:00:57.180 --> 00:00:58.180
summer.

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:01.039
The summertime residents are important for
keeping Amity a thriving community during

00:01:01.039 --> 00:01:04.420
the winter, since they mainly consist of lawyers
and bankers who are looking to get away for

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:05.420
twelve weeks.

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:08.899
There is this logic that all of the full-time
residents follow, where everyone does what

00:01:08.899 --> 00:01:11.159
they can to maintain a good image for the
town.

00:01:11.159 --> 00:01:14.299
That way, it always appears to be a favorable
place to spend the summers.

00:01:14.299 --> 00:01:18.149
This is done to produce a wealthy summer season
to get through the winter where, even after

00:01:18.149 --> 00:01:20.959
the best summers, three of every ten families
go on relief.

00:01:20.959 --> 00:01:24.530
Due to this understanding, the police chief,
Martin Brody, and the editor of the local

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:28.520
paper, Harry Meadows, will filter the news
to ensure that Amity appears attractive to

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:31.079
the summer people who subscribe to the local
paper.

00:01:31.079 --> 00:01:34.749
At the same time, the understanding roots
out anyone who is potentially dishonest in

00:01:34.749 --> 00:01:35.749
their work ethic.

00:01:35.749 --> 00:01:39.109
A few years before the novel, two brothers
came to Amity to start running a carpentry

00:01:39.109 --> 00:01:41.759
business and originally earned a good reputation.

00:01:41.759 --> 00:01:45.179
After the long-time residents discovered their
use of inferior parts, while charging for

00:01:45.179 --> 00:01:48.759
the higher quality ones, the people of Amity
made sure it was impossible for them to run

00:01:48.759 --> 00:01:49.759
the business.

00:01:49.759 --> 00:01:53.289
This unspoken agreement is stated to root
from a need to survive, meaning that one or

00:01:53.289 --> 00:01:55.840
two bad apples have to be tossed out as quickly
as possible.

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:58.789
If not, they could ruin the revenue for the
entire town.

00:01:58.789 --> 00:02:02.509
The Amity understanding is a portrayal of
how local and traditional mindsets function

00:02:02.509 --> 00:02:04.130
within modern limitations.

00:02:04.130 --> 00:02:08.219
The peaceful nature of the community is interrupted
when the shark appears in their waters.

00:02:08.219 --> 00:02:12.709
Measuring in at about 20 feet long, 4 feet
wide at the snout, and an estimated weight

00:02:12.709 --> 00:02:15.950
of 5,000-6,000 pounds, Jaws is bigger than
a large pick-up truck.

00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:20.459
This is slightly smaller than his film counterpart,
Bruce, who measured up to 25 feet.

00:02:20.459 --> 00:02:24.330
Jaws first emerges from the depths around
1:00AM on June 16th, nearly a whole month

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:25.330
before the movie.

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:28.849
He’s initially attracted to Amity’s beaches
by the vibrations of a late night swimmer,

00:02:28.849 --> 00:02:30.540
Christine ‘Chrissie’ Watkins.

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:34.120
Starting by making a wide circle around her,
the water briefly surges up before settling

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.120
back down.

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:37.459
Being alerted to something, she pauses for
a moment.

00:02:37.459 --> 00:02:41.239
Since she’s already tired and a bit uneasy,
she starts to hurry back to the shore.

00:02:41.239 --> 00:02:45.019
She initially believed some coral or driftwood
had scraped against her leg, but when she

00:02:45.019 --> 00:02:49.390
went to feel for her foot, she has to reach
higher and higher until her fingers found

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:50.969
the nub of her bone.

00:02:50.969 --> 00:02:52.989
Screaming in panic, she starts thrashing for the
shore.

00:02:52.989 --> 00:02:57.010
Taking his chance, Jaws dives down before
ramming into her from below and tossing her

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:58.010
out of the water.

00:02:58.010 --> 00:03:02.310
Clamping his mouth around her torso, he slams
back into the water in a shower of blood and

00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:03.680
scraps of flesh.

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:08.319
This seems to be the point that Jaws develops
a craving for human flesh, instead of… you

00:03:08.319 --> 00:03:11.920
know, just seals and fish and the Sunday deal
at Long John Silver’s.

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:15.720
A normal shark might have spat her leg out,
because people are too boney and don’t have

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:18.219
the amount of fat content that sharks prefer.

00:03:18.219 --> 00:03:21.870
Typically when sharks go for people it’s
because they’re starving or just confused

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:23.440
the person for a seal.

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:24.490
Or… you know.

00:03:24.490 --> 00:03:25.621
The Sunday deal at Long John--

00:03:25.621 --> 00:03:30.159
Rather than that, Jaws becomes the ‘monster’
of nightmares by deciding the waters of Amity

00:03:30.159 --> 00:03:32.180
are now part of its home range.

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:35.810
Adding this stop to its migration route probably means
that he’ll stick around anywhere

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:37.200
from 1 to 3 months.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:41.280
In doing this, he becomes the harbinger of
the residents' worst fears and revealer of

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:42.610
their darkest secrets.

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:46.579
Jaws becomes known as an unforgiving overlord
and gatekeeper of Amity.

00:03:46.579 --> 00:03:50.450
The initial response from Mayor Vaughn and
Meadows was to keep it quiet to ensure a good

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:54.000
summer revenue, despite Chief Brody’s insistence
to close the beaches.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:57.661
Their logic to keep them open is that it was
that the attack was a one-time thing, since

00:03:57.661 --> 00:04:00.189
sharks don’t usually stay in one place for
long.

00:04:00.189 --> 00:04:04.049
Chief Brody originally objects, arguing with
Mayor Vaughn that he has the interest of public

00:04:04.049 --> 00:04:05.049
safety in mind.

00:04:05.049 --> 00:04:07.740
However, he seems to be the only one for closing
the beaches.

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:11.359
With his job threatened by the Mayor, he concedes
and allows the beaches to stay open.

00:04:11.359 --> 00:04:15.829
The offensive nature of Vaughn’s position
appears to be justified, based on the Amity understanding.

00:04:15.829 --> 00:04:19.280
They still need the summer to go well for
the town to survive through winter.

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:23.300
Meanwhile, Chief Brody’s position initially
seems to come from his fear of the ocean,

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:25.460
and any water that is deeper than his shoulders.

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:29.620
In this sense, Jaws is the physical embodiment
of Chief Brody’s fear of the demons under

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:30.620
the water.

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:34.780
The next time Jaws surfaces is on Sunday,
June 20th when 6 year old Alex Kintner goes

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:36.350
out to swim on his small raft.

00:04:36.350 --> 00:04:40.610
The raft Alex is on is small enough for him
to use it similarly to a boogie board, or surfboard.

00:04:40.610 --> 00:04:44.400
He doesn’t notice the current carrying him
further from shore until he’s about 40 yards

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:45.400
away.

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:48.270
With his legs splashing in the water, the
shark hones in on the movement it stirs.

00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:52.250
Jaws follows the vibrations until he’s about
20 feet away, then there’s a brief moment

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:55.880
when he loses the signal, passing directly
under Alex as the boy takes a break.

00:04:55.880 --> 00:04:59.750
It’s not until Alex starts kicking again
that Jaws locks in on the source of the movement.

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:03.410
He propels himself almost straight out of
the water, knocking the child and raft into

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:04.410
his mouth.

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:07.360
I tried doing this at the Taco Bell drive
through, by just sticking my head out the

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:10.650
window and flooring it, but it didn’t go
quite how I imagined.

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:15.039
Unlike my taco, Alex’s death was quick,
and over with before the boy could scream.

00:05:15.039 --> 00:05:17.510
The only part of him not swallowed up was
his legs.

00:05:17.510 --> 00:05:21.349
As Jaws flops back into the ocean, Alex's
father on shore notices the movement.

00:05:21.349 --> 00:05:24.960
When he goes to Mrs. Kintner, the realization
takes a moment to set in.

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:27.539
Together, they go to the police station to
report the incident.

00:05:27.539 --> 00:05:31.470
Unfortunately for Amity, two reporters from
the New York Times and Newsday, respectively,

00:05:31.470 --> 00:05:33.280
happened to be at the beach.

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:37.110
They both inhabit the police station after
the event, trying to get information to publish

00:05:37.110 --> 00:05:38.110
 a story.

00:05:38.110 --> 00:05:39.840
This is one of the worst situations for Amity.

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:43.849
If the story got out, their 4th of July weekend
would be a bust, and potentially force the

00:05:43.849 --> 00:05:46.340
town into massive decline over the winter.

00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:49.930
With money already tight in most households,
a poor summer could lead to the townspeople

00:05:49.930 --> 00:05:53.699
buying cheaper goods, resulting in a declining
tax revenue, which would make it difficult

00:05:53.699 --> 00:05:56.840
to effectively maintain public works, like
gas and electricity.

00:05:56.840 --> 00:06:01.039
The domino effect could lead to long-time
residents moving out, turning Amity into a

00:06:01.039 --> 00:06:02.039
ghost town.

00:06:02.039 --> 00:06:06.060
In the middle of the exchange, another cop
named Patrolman Hendricks bursts in, frantically

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:10.460
informing Chief Brody of another attack, and
this one would be too gruesome to include

00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:11.561
in the movie.

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:23.830
After the patrolman’s outburst, Chief
Brody is silently thankful that the reporters

00:06:23.830 --> 00:06:27.139
failed to notice the slip of Hendricks’s
tongue with the word: another.

00:06:27.139 --> 00:06:30.349
Hendricks is the most up-to-speed on the shark
attacks, aside from the Chief, so a massive

00:06:30.349 --> 00:06:33.510
slip up could have jeopardized the reputation
of the town’s authorities.

00:06:33.510 --> 00:06:36.940
Urging him to continue, Hendricks describes
how he went to the beach for the first time

00:06:36.940 --> 00:06:40.310
in years, and heard a surfer scream as he
was repeatedly knocked down.

00:06:40.310 --> 00:06:43.350
He explained to Chief Brody that “…blood
was flying all over the place.

00:06:43.350 --> 00:06:46.009
The fish kept coming back and hitting him
again and again.”

00:06:46.009 --> 00:06:49.470
Hendricks had tried to go and help the man,
reaching waist-deep water, but by the time

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:52.860
he was able to grab the man’s hand, his
arm fell away from his shoulder.

00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:57.220
This type of attack pattern is generally used
by sharks for larger prey, like elephant seals,

00:06:57.220 --> 00:06:59.350
which can fight back and do damage to their
skin.

00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:02.700
The idea is to stun the prey, making it easier
to kill and consume.

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:06.629
We can only imagine the shark felt somewhat
intimidated by the sheer size of the man's

00:07:06.629 --> 00:07:09.889
surfboard, since boards usually range from
6 to 7 feet long.

00:07:09.889 --> 00:07:13.759
This surfer incident, on top of the Kintner
boy, causes Chief Brody to order the immediate

00:07:13.759 --> 00:07:16.889
closure of the beaches, to ensure public safety.

00:07:16.889 --> 00:07:18.319
Sounds all too familiar...

00:07:18.319 --> 00:07:21.639
When discussing the situation with Mayor Vaughn,
the two decide to hunt down the shark before

00:07:21.639 --> 00:07:23.159
it can do any further damage.

00:07:23.159 --> 00:07:27.561
On Tuesday June 24th, the local fisherman,
Ben Gardner, was sent out on his boat to look

00:07:27.561 --> 00:07:28.561
for Jaws.

00:07:28.561 --> 00:07:32.189
Chief Brody spends an hour watching his boat,
the Flicka, with binoculars until Hendricks

00:07:32.189 --> 00:07:33.920
shows up to see how things are going.

00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:37.419
Expressing his concern, the Chief decides
to head to the marina to borrow a boat with

00:07:37.419 --> 00:07:38.419
Hendricks.

00:07:38.419 --> 00:07:40.849
When they reach Gardner's boat, they can’t find
any sign of him.

00:07:40.849 --> 00:07:44.740
They look around and discover that the radio is still
on, and the boat anchored in at least a hundred

00:07:44.740 --> 00:07:45.740
feet of water.

00:07:45.740 --> 00:07:49.080
The only signs of what could have happened
are some scraped paint and what could have

00:07:49.080 --> 00:07:50.860
been a bite mark on the hull.

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:53.789
Noticing something in one of the punctures,
the Chief lifts Hendricks over the side.

00:07:53.789 --> 00:07:57.819
When he’s pulled back in the boat, Hendricks
reveals a two-inch wide shark tooth.

00:07:57.819 --> 00:08:01.009
The only conclusion they can come up with
is that Jaws got ahold of Ben somehow.

00:08:01.009 --> 00:08:04.979
It’s a reasonable one too, as there have
been documented instances of Great White sharks

00:08:04.979 --> 00:08:06.060
attacking fishing boats.

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:09.969
It’s a bit unclear why Jaws would attack
the boat, it could be that it saw the dropping

00:08:09.969 --> 00:08:13.810
anchor as a threat, or possibly
that he smelled fish and was curious about

00:08:13.810 --> 00:08:14.810
if he could eat the boat or not.

00:08:15.810 --> 00:08:18.310
When Sharks are on the prowl for food, they
usually take a bite first to see if they like

00:08:18.310 --> 00:08:21.840
it, and if it doesn’t taste like something
in their usual diet, they usually just leave

00:08:21.840 --> 00:08:22.840
it.

00:08:22.840 --> 00:08:26.229
But if this impact knocked Ben into the water,
Jaws might have just taken that as his reward

00:08:26.229 --> 00:08:30.009
instead, remember, this particular shark seems
to have actually developed a taste for humans.

00:08:30.009 --> 00:08:33.480
By now, Jaws knows a few things about the
waters around Amity.

00:08:33.480 --> 00:08:36.890
First is that there’s always food around,
even on boats, and that people count as a

00:08:36.890 --> 00:08:38.280
tasty food source.

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:41.480
With Ben Gardner’s death, we are introduced
to the ichthyologist, Matt Hooper.

00:08:41.480 --> 00:08:44.270
Basically, Hooper studies sharks and frequently
dives with them.

00:08:44.270 --> 00:08:47.980
He’s described as being clean shaven, tanned,
lean, and being in his mid-twenties.

00:08:47.980 --> 00:08:52.140
So, nothing like the bearded depiction in
the film because supposedly having a big beard like

00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:54.020
that can get in the way while diving.

00:08:54.020 --> 00:08:57.350
Another differing point from the film is that
Chief Brody has an immediate dislike towards

00:08:57.350 --> 00:08:58.350
Hooper.

00:08:58.350 --> 00:09:01.450
While they’re on good terms on screen, their
novel depictions frequently get into arguments

00:09:01.450 --> 00:09:02.660
over almost everything.

00:09:02.660 --> 00:09:06.750
In the wake of Hooper’s arrival and Ben’s
death, Hooper begins using the Flicka to patrol

00:09:06.750 --> 00:09:07.750
the waters.

00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:10.820
With the beaches still closed, he’s able
to test the water and study the marine life

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:12.950
in hopes of finding out why Jaws is there.

00:09:12.950 --> 00:09:16.650
Unfortunately for Hooper, he doesn’t run
into the shark after spending an entire week

00:09:16.650 --> 00:09:17.840
studying the area.

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:21.340
So, when he attends the meeting of the selectmen,
Mayor Vaughn and Chief Brody, he confirms

00:09:21.340 --> 00:09:24.710
that they should be clear to reopen the beaches
for the 4th of July weekend.

00:09:24.710 --> 00:09:27.760
He also notes that the water is getting too
warm for a Great White to be there.

00:09:27.760 --> 00:09:31.080
The Chief doesn’t want anything reopened,
claiming that they don’t know if the shark

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:32.380
actually left or not.

00:09:32.380 --> 00:09:36.020
Despite his initial feeling, the selectmen
and the Mayor point out that the town is

00:09:36.020 --> 00:09:37.020
dying.

00:09:37.020 --> 00:09:39.580
The past two weeks have had a major impact
on local businesses, forcing many to have

00:09:39.580 --> 00:09:42.200
sales just to scrape in a little bit of profit.

00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:45.890
With the beaches open for the holiday weekend,
Chief Brody sets Hendricks up on the public

00:09:45.890 --> 00:09:49.820
beach, Hooper out in Flicka, and himself on
the private beaches to keep watch for any

00:09:49.820 --> 00:09:50.820
sign of the shark.

00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:55.450
On July 3rd the Chief encountered a family
trespassing on the private beaches.

00:09:55.450 --> 00:09:58.700
In their conversation, he discovers that Amity
is getting a reputation for having a killer

00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:00.320
shark inhabiting the waters.

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:03.770
The family came to the beach hoping to get
a glimpse, and this was the exact opposite

00:10:03.770 --> 00:10:05.700
of what Amity wants to be known for.

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:09.290
While having a man-eating shark will keep
a lot of tourist money away, there are some

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:13.340
people who would travel out of their way to
see these… interesting creatures.

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:14.990
Even if that means risking their life.

00:10:15.990 --> 00:10:16.990
What?

00:10:16.990 --> 00:10:18.590
Why are you looking at me like that?

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:22.590
However, the town would end up nearly completely
abandoned before shark spotting would become

00:10:22.590 --> 00:10:24.060
its main point of interest.

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:26.430
The bad luck in Amity doesn’t seem to run
out.

00:10:26.430 --> 00:10:29.950
All it takes to stir up a sense of unease
is for a young boy to go swimming, on a bet.

00:10:29.950 --> 00:10:34.760
And the shark would not be Brody’s only
worry, with a news reporter also prowling

00:10:34.760 --> 00:10:36.460
on the scene of this summertime getaway.

00:10:36.460 --> 00:10:38.620
Brody keeps an eye out for the boy as he goes
out.

00:10:38.620 --> 00:10:42.670
It doesn’t take long for Hooper to see something
in the water and quickly turn the boat around.

00:10:42.670 --> 00:10:45.850
Radioing Hooper, the Chief tells him about
the boy so he can move the boat closer.

00:10:45.850 --> 00:10:50.160
What they don’t know is that Jaws was hanging
around underneath the Flicka for most of the

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:51.160
day.

00:10:51.160 --> 00:10:53.940
The change in the boat’s motor, brings the
shark to life, causing it to follow the boat

00:10:53.940 --> 00:10:56.430
towards shallower water, and towards the boy.

00:10:56.430 --> 00:10:59.580
Chief Brody moves into the water a bit, getting
knocked back by a wave.

00:10:59.580 --> 00:11:03.140
As the boy reaches the chest-deep water and
tries moving further towards shore, the fin

00:11:03.140 --> 00:11:05.710
of the shark appears out of the water behind
him.

00:11:05.710 --> 00:11:09.070
Between the Chief and the shark, the boy moves
a bit faster because he knows something is

00:11:09.070 --> 00:11:10.070
wrong.

00:11:10.070 --> 00:11:13.730
In a stroke of luck, Chief Brody gets the
boy first and Jaws retreats deeper into the water.

00:11:13.730 --> 00:11:17.230
While this scene is tense, it does display
natural limitations of the shark.

00:11:17.230 --> 00:11:21.340
Since he has to continuously move forward in order to breathe,
he has to avoid accidentally beaching himself

00:11:21.340 --> 00:11:24.830
over a mouthful of food, so the shallower
areas were essentially off-limits.

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:28.690
Forced to close the beaches again, Amity has
to come up with another solution.

00:11:28.690 --> 00:11:32.940
In a last ditch effort, they call in a former
War veteran turned sharkhunter named Sam Quint,

00:11:32.940 --> 00:11:36.270
a man who takes the cliche ‘swears like
a sailor’ to the extreme.

00:11:36.270 --> 00:11:39.040
I’d love for him to meet our cab driver
from It.

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:43.530
With the new ally came a new boat, but even
with a bigger boat, Jaws was unafraid to back

00:11:43.530 --> 00:11:44.700
down from the challenge.

00:11:44.700 --> 00:11:48.692
“We’re gonna need a bigger boat.”

00:11:56.301 --> 00:12:00.540
On Quint’s boat, Orca, they manage to encounter
Jaws a total of three times.

00:12:00.540 --> 00:12:02.310
The first time is only a brief passing.

00:12:02.310 --> 00:12:06.160
The second time, Hooper hops into his shark
cage to see Jaws underwater and take some

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:07.160
photos.

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:10.240
When he goes in, he takes an underwater weapon
in case Jaws gets too close.

00:12:10.240 --> 00:12:14.277
On the initial pass, Jaws swims close enough
to the cage for Hooper to run his hand along

00:12:14.277 --> 00:12:14.870
the side.

00:12:14.870 --> 00:12:19.020
The interaction is peaceful, until the sounds
of Quint firing shots into the water disturb

00:12:19.020 --> 00:12:20.020
the scene.

00:12:20.020 --> 00:12:23.438
Once this happens, Jaws swims out a bit before
turning and ramming himself into the cage.

00:12:26.193 --> 00:12:30.230
He manages to pry the bars apart with his
continued ramming, the same technique used

00:12:30.230 --> 00:12:32.580
against elephant seals and more dangerous
prey.

00:12:32.580 --> 00:12:36.310
It seems that Jaws didn’t truly feel threatened
until the shots were fired at him.

00:12:36.310 --> 00:12:40.480
The disturbance agitated him to some degree,
and he associated it with the strange cage

00:12:40.480 --> 00:12:41.480
floating nearby.

00:12:41.480 --> 00:12:45.250
The Hooper in the novel isn’t as fortunate
as his film counterpart.

00:12:45.250 --> 00:12:47.830
Before he’s able to use the weapon, the
shark bites down on his torso.

00:12:47.830 --> 00:12:52.610
In a display of… graphic details, Jaws jumps
out of the water with Hooper’s legs hanging

00:12:52.610 --> 00:12:55.320
out of one side of his mouth, and his head
and arms out the other.

00:12:55.320 --> 00:12:59.810
I guess Mrs. Jaws never taught her son PROPER
MANNERS AT THE DINNER TABLE.

00:12:59.810 --> 00:13:03.050
With Hooper dead, Quint declares that this
hunt is no longer a matter of money.

00:13:03.050 --> 00:13:06.370
Though he never speaks the reason, it seems
clear that he has developed a burning desire

00:13:06.370 --> 00:13:08.830
to kill it, even if he has to do it alone.

00:13:08.830 --> 00:13:12.500
Their final encounter with Jaws turns into
a storied hunt that the novel has led up

00:13:12.500 --> 00:13:13.500
to.

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:17.270
Once they get to a specific area closer to
shore, Jaws surfaces as if waiting for them.

00:13:17.270 --> 00:13:21.270
Within a half hour, Quint and Brody manage
to hook 3 harpoons, into him: one by his fin,

00:13:21.270 --> 00:13:24.150
another near his stomach, and one in the head,
just above the right eye.

00:13:24.150 --> 00:13:28.020
During this, Jaws attempts to sink their boat
by ramming into it, even taking a bite to

00:13:28.020 --> 00:13:29.080
shake the boat.

00:13:29.080 --> 00:13:33.210
Eventually, Jaws resorts to trying to swim
away for nearly 3 hours, dragging the vessel

00:13:33.210 --> 00:13:34.420
with him as he goes.

00:13:34.420 --> 00:13:38.020
When the barrels stop moving, Quint takes
them in close to lasso Jaws’ tail and attempt

00:13:38.020 --> 00:13:42.170
to hoist him on the winch, but Jaws turns
in a last ditch effort to escape and crashes

00:13:42.170 --> 00:13:45.300
onto the deck, and the impact is enough to
start sinking the boat.

00:13:45.300 --> 00:13:49.550
In a mad fit of fury, Quint takes a harpoon
and stabs the shark in the gut, deep enough

00:13:49.550 --> 00:13:51.620
for blood to cover his hand.

00:13:51.620 --> 00:13:54.891
When Jaws rolls back into the water, Quint’s
leg gets caught in the rope tethered to the

00:13:54.891 --> 00:13:56.720
harpoon, and he’s pulled overboard.

00:13:56.720 --> 00:14:00.610
Jaws is simply trying to get back in the water
to be able to breath, but it causes Quint

00:14:00.610 --> 00:14:02.580
to end up drowning from his own slip up.

00:14:02.580 --> 00:14:03.580
Pretty brutal way to go.

00:14:03.580 --> 00:14:05.210
But not as much as the movie though, roll
that ****.

00:14:18.600 --> 00:14:22.730
Luckily for Chief Brody, he doesn’t need
a gun or an oxygen tank to save himself.

00:14:22.730 --> 00:14:26.940
In the end, Jaws is merely a mortal shark
and dies from his injuries just before getting

00:14:26.940 --> 00:14:28.620
the chance to take a bite out of Brody.

00:14:28.620 --> 00:14:32.410
The last we see of Jaws is him sinking back
towards the depths of the ocean.

00:14:32.410 --> 00:14:36.420
In the end, Jaws terrorized the people of
Amity and their summer visitors for nearly

00:14:36.420 --> 00:14:37.450
an entire month.

00:14:37.450 --> 00:14:41.320
The six victims taken were not the only way
that the creature wreaked havoc on citizens

00:14:41.320 --> 00:14:44.860
though, as it potentially ruined the entire
summer season economy, making the upcoming

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:45.930
winter more difficult.

00:14:45.930 --> 00:14:50.410
While the film shows Jaws as a ruthless killer,
the novel reveals a more realistic depiction

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:54.740
of a shark with some tendencies we can analyse
and understand, and others that can still

00:14:54.740 --> 00:14:56.040
not be explained.

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:59.670
Hopefully this analysis helps add a layer
of reality behind the ocean dwelling terror

00:14:59.670 --> 00:15:00.970
that is Jaws.

00:15:00.970 --> 00:15:04.540
And by the way, let me know of any other creatures
you’d like to see covered here on Horror

00:15:04.540 --> 00:15:06.850
History, or what franchise you’d like to
see me take on.

00:15:06.850 --> 00:15:11.170
Remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for new
horrors every week, ring the deathbell for

00:15:11.170 --> 00:15:14.060
notifications and I’ll see you in the next
one.

00:15:14.060 --> 00:15:15.630
Assuming we both survive.

